abstract: >
  TIDE (Temporal Index of Divergent Evidence) measures semantic drift between a
  fixed recommendation anchor and its year-binned PubMed
  literature using biomedical text embeddings (MedCPT). For each recommendation it
  computes the annual mean cosine similarity between the recommendation and the
  contemporary abstracts, then tests for a monotonic temporal trend (Kendall tau).
  This public repository contains frozen queries, PMID mappings, cached embeddings,
  numerical results and analysis scripts for a three-case proof of concept in orthopedic surgery
  (periprosthetic joint infection, acute compartment syndrome, and distal radius
  fracture). It is a proof of concept and makes no claim of generalizability,
  predictive accuracy, sensitivity, or specificity. Article text is excluded;
  text-dependent reproduction requires a separately retained frozen archive.

keywords:
  - clinical practice guidelines
  - semantic drift
  - evidence surveillance
  - natural language processing
  - biomedical text embeddings
  - MedCPT
  - orthopedic surgery
  - PubMed

